{
 "version": 1,
 "name": "DE_4546B designed planet (S8a Stage C, 2026-10-23): Subnautica's biome layout around the authentic crater, scaled x3 to a 12 km ring, then the Crater Edge down to the void floor (design 4: no dead zone)",
 "notes": [
  "Authored by hand from the public shape of Subnautica's map (north +z, east +x); nothing of the game is read.",
  "Coordinates of seeds, canyons and the island are MAP metres (the Subnautica map); the planet takes them times 'scale' in SN metres around the site (site v1).",
  "Every biome region is the nearest-seed (Voronoi) cell of its seeds after a fixed warp; heights blend between neighbouring biomes over 'softM' map metres.",
  "layoutSeed shapes everything (regions, relief, ores); the tool's --seed changes only the small detail layer ('detail': boulders and ripples of +-2 m), never the layout.",
  "snName is the biome name Subnautica's GetBiome returns there (S8aMaterialMap.BiomeNames, CONTRACT biome.names); the material map's G channel holds its index + 1.",
  "Owner play 2026-10-23 ('c'est juste flat'): hills (10-20 m every 100-300 m) and boulder fields scale with each biome's 'relief'; biome boundaries step by up to cliffM (a cliff within ~cliffSoftM map metres) and ramp the rest over softM; the heightmap pixel is 46 m, so nothing finer than about 100 m exists in SE's heightmap.",
  "Materials are CustomMaterialTable subtypes (Sand_02 1, Stone_01 2, Stone_02 3, Stone_03 4, Stone_04 5, Stone_05 6, Grass 7): 'flat' below 'slopeMin', 'slope' above it.",
  "ores.rows: the depth-rarity table (seabed depth band, biomes, share of the eligible seabed, patch size); Start/DepthBelow are SE's OreMappings Start/Depth (metres below the surface).",
  "Design 4 (owner free play 2026-10-23 22:xx: 'je veux une continuite, pas de dead zone'): no moat and no void floor; the ring's outer Crater Edge drops to a trough (planet.edgeRise.troughDepthM) whose floor rises over riseM, from the end of the ring's region, into a continuous slope to the planet shelf; the planet is mostly shelf 40-120 m (basins.shelfLevel), reefs and slopes 150-400 m, deep basins (planet.deepBasins) and trenches only where those biomes are, with the deep looks (Grand Reef, Blood Kelp)."
 ],
